#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Equilibrium acceptance corpora on two prepared environments; one table (docs/agents/workflow.md "Gates").

Runs, in each selected environment, the Cameretti 2005 bubble states (default start), the
Gross 2002 declarations (default start), the 70-case neutral methane/ethane sweep, the #243 42-row
matrix, four-section replay and declared 73-state MEA flash family, then compares B with A. Cases a gate already runs (the #390 and
#407 pins, e4-d, the Gross pins in equilibrium/Automatic*) are omitted. Work counts, timings,
messages and diagnostic residuals are reported by the scripts, not compared here; every other value
must be finite on both sides and agree within 1e-10 relative (absolute floor 1e-12), with equal text
and JSON kinds. Gross deviation and percent columns are reported, not compared: they are functions of
the compared value and its input reference, and amplify last-bit changes (owner, 2026-10-13). Both sides must reproduce the accepted inventories and successes (ACCEPTED), every
criterion must be finite and positive, and every successful result must have a finite residual within
its own criterion (Gross: calculation.json row_tolerance; Cameretti: run.py's criterion-violations.csv
must have no rows, and each band's largest declared residual must be within its largest criterion).
The replay uses replay_compare.py's checks and quantity limits. The MEA family requires 73/73 successes
in both images, the 1e-10 row criterion, and entrywise abs(a-b)/max(abs(a),abs(b),1e-14) <= 1e-10
for amounts, fractions and densities; its work and timing are diagnostic. Exits 1 on any problem or failed job.
Tracked results/ are never written.
"""
